<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:orl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Logging;assembly=OpenRigs.Logging"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>A task's logs on ZapitDaq (TaskLogs is MATLAB Zapit's), the same in every task: the input, the task file read at Go as JSON (TaskConfig through the task's own SerializeToJson), as Settings_Task; once the experiment folder exists (PathPrefix), WorkflowData_Trials (LogTrials of TrialRow, one row per trial); and each of ZapitDaq's events (Zapit.Events: BankLoaded, Armed, Started, Ended, Stopped, Zeroed, Pointed, Refused) as an Events row (Event Zapit, Detail the kind, trial, condition, laser, power asked and capped, arm time, samples generated of the trial's samples, and last the event's detail (the bank's path, or why it was refused), Value the trial), on the Harp clock, into WorkflowData_Events (LogEvents keeps rows sent before the experiment folder exists). The bank, sample, scanner frames and conditions copy are the agent's files. A task's other logs stay in the task. It has no output: an include ends its side branches when its output completes, and Settings_Task completes at Go, which ended the trial and Zapit logs before trial 1. Needs TrialRow, TaskConfig, Zapit.Events, Events, Timestamp and PathPrefix from the workflow.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
        <Name>Source1</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogDataSchema.bonsai">
        <Name>Settings_Task</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
        <Name>TrialLogs</Name>
        <Description>The trial log, once the experiment folder exists (PathPrefix): WorkflowData_Trials.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRow</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogTrials.bonsai" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
        <scr:Name>ZapitEventRow</scr:Name>
        <scr:Expression>new(Kind.ToString() + " trial " + Trial.ToString() + " condition " + Condition.ToString() + " laserOn " + LaserOn.ToString() + " powerMw " + PowerMw.ToString() + " cappedPowerMw " + CappedPowerMw.ToString() + " powerCapped " + PowerCapped.ToString() + " armSeconds " + ArmSeconds.ToString() + " samples " + SamplesGenerated.ToString() + "/" + Samples.ToString() + " detail " + Detail as Detail, Trial as Value)</scr:Expression>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orl:CreateEvent">
          <orl:Event>Zapit</orl:Event>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="Bonsai.Harp:WithLatestTimestamp.bonsai">
        <Name>Timestamp</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Events</Name>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
